WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.846
Now that we have a little familiarity with the OSI model, let's look at some devices, protocols, and applications and see which layers are used for these on the OSI model.

00:08.846 --> 00:20.110
On Application layer we see HTTP, SMTP, DNS, basically anything controlling an app or service, but not the app or service itself.

00:20.110 --> 00:27.409
Thus, while HTTP is on this Application layer, a web browser is not.

00:27.409 --> 00:40.422
Presentation covers formatting, like HTML, JPEG, GIF, and encryption happens at this layer as well. Session layer we usually see protocols like NetBIOS.

00:40.422 --> 00:53.728
Transport layer has protocols such as TCP, UDP, and IP. The Network layer has routers and layer 3 switches. The Data-link layer, layer 2 switches.

00:53.728 --> 00:58.399
And the Physical layer, hubs, Ethernet, and network cables.

00:58.399 --> 01:08.076
Another way to look at this is that layers 1 through 3 are hardware layers, while layers 4 through 7 are mainly protocol-based.

